# profile_pocket_rough.cam — the wall-only roughing fixture, both comp modes in one
# golden (the cylinder_rough.cam two-run pattern). The finishing sibling is
# profile_pocket.cam; the two differ by exactly the stock_to_leave field.
#
# A Contour cuts one surface — a wall — and the allowance is radial, so the
# whole 0.5mm becomes offset and the cusp budget is structurally 0.000: a single
# pass at one Z has no adjacent pair to leave a cusp between.
#
# The Window loop is wound CCW, so the tool cuts INSIDE it (the winding
# convention, DECISIONS.md "Row-2.4 `side` selector") and leaving stock means
# the wall closes IN on the tool: every emitted coordinate moves 0.5mm toward
# the centre versus profile_pocket.cam.
#
# Hand-checked anchors (60mm square from 20 to 80, T5 dia 10 so r = 5):
#   - engine comp offsets by r + skin = 5.5 inward, so the emitted tool-centre
#     path runs 25.5 .. 74.5 (profile_pocket.cam emits 25 .. 75).
#   - control comp emits the PART EDGE, not the tool centre, and bakes only the
#     skin into it: 20.5 .. 79.5 (the authored 20 .. 80 shrunk by 0.5). The D
#     register stays D5 — the pure tool radius — so the controller adds r on top
#     and the metal lands in the same place as the engine pass. Baking the
#     allowance into D instead would be a double-comp waiting to happen, which
#     is why finish_cylinder set this precedent and why it holds here.
units mm
feed 800
plunge 300
rapid_z 5
clearance_z 25
spindle 3000

stock Box(w=100, l=100, h=20, x=0, y=0, z=0)

tool T5 Endmill(dia=10.0)

feature Window ProfilePocket(extent=2.0
    20 20
    80 20
    80 80
    20 80
)

run Side(tool=T5, surface=Window, stock_to_leave=0.5)
run Side(tool=T5, surface=Window, comp=control, stock_to_leave=0.5)
